Keep the compiler cache variables in the captured Windows environment.

On Windows the generated ninja file runs every compile through "ninja -t msvc -e
environment.<arch>", which replaces the whole environment with the block gyp
captured when it generated the build. That block keeps only the variables the
Visual Studio toolchain itself needs, so a compiler cache put in front of cl.exe
starts with no home directory and no configuration:

 ccache: error: The USERPROFILE environment variable must be set to your user
 profile folder

Keeping USERPROFILE and the CCACHE_ variables lets the cache find its home and
the shared cache directory the build was told to use.

--- a/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
+++ b/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
@@ -1101,6 +1101,7 @@
     """Extracts environment variables required for the toolchain to run from
     a textual dump output by the cmd.exe 'set' command."""
     envvars_to_save = (
+        "ccache_.*",
         "goma_.*",  # TODO(scottmg): This is ugly, but needed for goma.
         "include",
         "lib",
@@ -1110,6 +1111,7 @@
         "systemroot",
         "temp",
         "tmp",
+        "userprofile",
     )
     env = {}
     # This occasionally happens and leads to misleading SYSTEMROOT error messages
